---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Ozee, explaining how personal data is processed on this website."
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden pt-40 pb-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6">
      <p class="reveal text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-brand-soft/80 mb-4">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="reveal text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="reveal text-white/50 mb-10">Last updated: August 8, 2026</p>

      <div class="reveal text-white/70 leading-relaxed space-y-10">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-white/90 font-semibold mb-2">1. Controller</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            The controller responsible for the processing of personal data on this website is:
          </p>
          <p>
            Adrian Stapper<br />
            Artist name: Ozee<br />
            Denniweg 1<br />
            77830 Bühlertal<br />
            Germany
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Email: <a href="mailto:ozeemusic.contact@gmail.com" class="hover:text-brand-soft transition-colors">ozeemusic.contact@gmail.com</a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-white/90 font-semibold mb-2">2. General Information</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            I take the protection of your personal data seriously. This Privacy Policy explains
            what personal data may be processed when you visit this website and how I handle
            that data.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Personal data means any information relating to an identified or identifiable
            individual.
          </p>
          <p>
            I process personal data in accordance with applicable data protection laws, in
            particular the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-white/90 font-semibold mb-2">3. Hosting and Server Log Files</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            When you visit this website, technical information may be automatically transmitted
            to and temporarily stored by my hosting provider. This may include:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mb-3">
            <li>IP address</li>
            <li>date and time of access</li>
            <li>requested page or file</li>
            <li>browser type and version</li>
            <li>operating system</li>
            <li>referrer URL</li>
            <li>other technical information required to operate and secure the website</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mb-3">
            I process this data to ensure the secure and reliable operation of my website and to
            detect and prevent technical problems or misuse.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            The legal basis for this processing is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. My legitimate interest is
            the secure, stable and technically functional operation of my website.
          </p>
          <p>
            Server log data is generally deleted when it is no longer required for these
            purposes, unless longer retention is required for legal reasons.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-white/90 font-semibold mb-2">4. Google Analytics</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            I use Google Analytics, a web analytics service provided by Google Ireland Limited,
            Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            I use Google Analytics to analyse how visitors use my website and to understand and
            improve its content and performance.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">Google Analytics may process information such as:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mb-3">
            <li>IP address</li>
            <li>information about the device and browser used</li>
            <li>pages visited and interactions with the website</li>
            <li>approximate geographical information</li>
            <li>date and time of access</li>
            <li>information about the source from which you reached my website</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mb-6">
            Google Analytics may use cookies and similar technologies to collect this
            information.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-white/80 font-semibold mb-2">Legal basis</h3>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Google Analytics is only activated if you have provided your consent through the
            cookie consent mechanism on my website.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            The legal basis for processing personal data through Google Analytics is therefore
            Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR (consent).
          </p>
          <p class="mb-6">
            You may withdraw your consent at any time by opening the{' '}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="cookie-settings-link underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-brand-soft transition-colors cursor-pointer"
            >
              Cookie Settings
            </button>{' '}
            available on my website and changing your preferences. The withdrawal of consent does
            not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before the withdrawal.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-white/80 font-semibold mb-2">Google as a recipient of data</h3>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Depending on the configuration of Google Analytics and the applicable Google
            services, personal data may be transferred to and processed by Google entities
            outside the European Economic Area (EEA), including in countries such as the United
            States.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Google uses appropriate safeguards for international data transfers where required
            by applicable data protection law.
          </p>
          <p>
            For more information about how Google processes personal data, please refer to
            Google's Privacy Policy.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-white/90 font-semibold mb-2">5. Cookies</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">This website uses cookies and similar technologies.</p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Some cookies may be technically necessary for the operation of my website. Other
            cookies, such as those used by Google Analytics, are only used where you have given
            your consent.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            When you first visit my website, you can choose whether to consent to the use of
            non-essential cookies through the cookie consent banner.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can change or withdraw your consent at any time through the{' '}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="cookie-settings-link underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-brand-soft transition-colors cursor-pointer"
            >
              Cookie Settings
            </button>{' '}
            available on my website.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-white/90 font-semibold mb-2">6. Your Rights</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            Under the GDPR, you have various rights regarding your personal data. Depending on
            the circumstances, these include:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 mb-3">
            <li>
              <span class="text-white/90">Right of access</span> – You may request information
              about whether and how I process your personal data.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-white/90">Right to rectification</span> – You may request
              correction of inaccurate or incomplete personal data.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-white/90">Right to erasure</span> – You may request deletion of
              your personal data where the legal requirements are met.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-white/90">Right to restriction of processing</span> – You may
              request that the processing of your personal data be restricted in certain
              circumstances.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-white/90">Right to data portability</span> – Where applicable, you
              have the right to receive personal data you have provided to me in a structured,
              commonly used and machine-readable format.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-white/90">Right to object</span> – You may object to certain
              processing of your personal data where the legal requirements are met.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-white/90">Right to withdraw consent</span> – Where processing is
              based on your consent, you may withdraw that consent at any time. Withdrawal does
              not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before the withdrawal.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mb-3">
            To exercise your rights, please contact me using the email address provided above.
          </p>
          <p>
            You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a competent data protection
            supervisory authority.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-white/90 font-semibold mb-2">7. Third-Party Services and External Links</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            My website may contain links to external websites, music streaming platforms, social
            media profiles or other third-party services.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you follow such a link, you leave my website. The respective third party is
            responsible for the processing of your personal data on its platform. I recommend
            reviewing the privacy policy of the respective provider.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-white/90 font-semibold mb-2">8. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            I may update this Privacy Policy where necessary to reflect changes to my website,
            the services I use or applicable legal requirements.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3">
            The current version of this Privacy Policy is always available on my website.
          </p>
          <p>Last updated: August 8, 2026</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.cookie-settings-link').forEach((el) => {
    el.addEventListener('click', () => {
      window.dispatchEvent(new Event('open-cookie-settings'));
    });
  });
</script>
